{{/*
  review_ask_box: the author's box for their own removed report (quick
  261118-rz6, owner 2026-11-18). It opens from the bell row "Your report was
  removed after review." or "Your report stays removed." and from the same rows
  of the full updates list, on phone and laptop. It is the Log out box: the
  .logout-confirm classes of auth.css. updates.js fills and opens it, puts focus
  on the title with no button outlined, and only its buttons close it.

  Few words, nothing more: the title, the Why line from the server (none when no
  reason was recorded), then one of three states. Can ask: the Note (optional)
  box, at most 200 characters with no placeholder, Close and Ask for review.
  Asked and waiting: Asked. and Close. Three asks used: No asks left. and Close.
  After an ask, focus moves to the state line shown, so it is read out.
  It never shows the report's words, flag counts, who flagged, places or the
  moderator.

  Every page that loads updates.js includes it as a direct child of the body,
  never inside the bell dropdown, so no scrolling or clipped parent can cut it
  off on iPhone Safari.
*/}}
  <dialog id="review-ask-box" class="logout-confirm review-ask" aria-labelledby="review-ask-title">
    <div class="logout-confirm__body">
      <h2 class="logout-confirm__title" id="review-ask-title" tabindex="-1">Removed</h2>
      <p class="review-ask__why" id="review-ask-why" hidden></p>
      <div class="review-ask__note" id="review-ask-form" hidden>
        <label for="review-ask-note">Note (optional)</label>
        <textarea id="review-ask-note" maxlength="200" rows="3" autocomplete="off"></textarea>
      </div>
      <p class="review-ask__state" id="review-ask-asked" tabindex="-1" hidden>Asked.</p>
      <p class="review-ask__state" id="review-ask-none" tabindex="-1" hidden>No asks left.</p>
      <p class="inline-error" id="review-ask-error" role="alert" data-failed="Couldn't send. Try again." hidden></p>
      <div class="logout-confirm__actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn" id="review-ask-close">Close</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="review-ask-send" hidden>Ask for review</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
